</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1086/301885</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC1377164</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">9585613</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Houdayer C, Caux-Moncoutier V, Krieger S, Barrois M, Bonnet F, Bourdon V, et al. Guidelines for splicing analysis in molecular diagnosis derived from a set of 327 combined in silico/in vitro studies on BRCA1 and BRCA2 variants. Hum Mutat. 2012;33:1228&#x2013;38.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1002/humu.22101</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">22505045</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Infante M, Dur&#xe1;n M, Lasa A, Acedo A, De La Hoya M, Esteban-Carde&#xf1;osa E, et al. Two founder <i>BRCA2</i> mutations predispose to breast cancer in young women. Breast Cancer Res Treat. 2010;122:567&#x2013;71.
