rence><Reference><Citation>Buleje J, Guevara-Fujita M, Acosta O, Huaman FDP, Danos P, Murillo A, et al. Mutational analysis of BRCA1 and BRCA2 genes in Peruvian families with hereditary breast and ovarian cancer. Mol Genet Genomic Med (2017) 5(5). doi: 10.1002/mgg3.301</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.1002/mgg3.301</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC5606899</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">28944232</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Shao F, Duan Y, Zhao Y, Li Y, Liu J, Zhang C, et al. PARP inhibitors in breast and ovarian cancer with BRCA mutations: a meta-analysis of survival. Aging (2021) 13(6):8975&#x2013;88. doi: 10.18632/aging.202724</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.18632/aging.202724</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC8034970</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">33705352</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Pinto JA, Pinillos L, Villarreal-Garza C, Morante Z, Villar&#xe1;n MV, Mej&#xed;a G, et al. Barriers in Latin America for the management of locally advanced breast cancer. Ecancermedicalscience (2019) 13. doi: 10.3332/ecancer.2019.897</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3332/ecancer.2019.897</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC6372299</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">30792814</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Horgan D, Mia R, Erhabor T, Hamdi Y, Dandara C, Lal JA, et al. Fighting cancer around the world: A framework for action. Healthc (Basel) (2022) 10(11). doi: 10.3390/healthcare10112125</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="doi">10.3390/healthcare10112125</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC9690702</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">36360466</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Rebbeck TR, Friebel TM, Friedman E, Hamann U, Huo D, Kwong A, et al. Mutational spectrum in a worldwide study of 29,700 families with BRCA1 or BRCA2 mutations. Hum Mutat (2018) 39(5):593&#x2013;620. doi